Realists explain these failures as an inherent
consequence of the anarchic international
system and the power-driven nature of global
politics. For realists, the UNSC’s inability to act
decisively in Syria, Ukraine, or Gaza
demonstrates how the organisation is
ultimately subordinate to the interests of its
most powerful members. In the Syrian conflict,
for instance, Russia’s vetoes protected its ally,
the Assad regime and prevented any effective
collective action.
Liberals view the UNSC’s failures as a
challenge to the principles of multilateralism
