liberal thought. They argue that the paralysis of
the UNSC in conflicts such as Syria, Ukraine,
and Gaza results from structural flaws,
including the veto power of the P5, which
allows individual states to block collective
action. Liberals would highlight the need for
institutional reform, such as limiting veto power
