Power and Developments
The Influence of the Shift to a More Multipolar World Order on Global Stability
The global political order has shifted from the unipolar dominance of the United States following
the Cold War to a more multipolar system, with the rise of powers like China, India, Russia, and
regional blocs like the European Union. This shift has led to both opportunities and challenges
for global stability. While multipolarity offers a more balanced distribution of power, it also
increases the potential for rivalry and conflict among major powers. Examples include the
growing tensions between the United States and China, Russia’s resurgence in Eastern Europe,
and regional disputes in Asia and the Middle East.
