Liberals view the United States’ global role as
integral to the liberal international order it
helped create after World War II. They argue
that U.S. leadership in international institutions,
such as the United Nations and Bretton Woods
system, has been essential for maintaining
global stability and promoting values like
democracy, human rights, and free trade.
While acknowledging the challenges to U.S.
